    S:TileEntity_DESCRIPTION_09405_Index_07=During operation, will consume ALL §fPolyaluminium Chloride§7 in the input hatch
    S:TileEntity_DESCRIPTION_09405_Index_08=At the end of the recipe, for every §c100000L §7of §fPolyaluminium Chloride§7 consumed
    S:TileEntity_DESCRIPTION_09405_Index_09=gain an additive §c10.0%§7 increase to success. If total fluid supplied is not
    S:TileEntity_DESCRIPTION_09405_Index_10=a multiple of §c100000L§7, a penalty to success is applied using the following formula:
    S:TileEntity_DESCRIPTION_09405_Index_11=§aSuccess = Success * 2^(-10 * Overflow ratio)
    S:TileEntity_DESCRIPTION_09405_Index_12=§7§m-----------------------------------------
    S:TileEntity_DESCRIPTION_09405_Index_13=§b§oStep three in purifying water is to remove microscopic contaminants such as dusts, microplastics and other
    S:TileEntity_DESCRIPTION_09405_Index_14=§b§opollutants using a clarifying agent (In this case, polyaluminium chloride) to cause flocculation - the process
    S:TileEntity_DESCRIPTION_09405_Index_15=§b§oof aggregating dispersed suspended particles from a solution into larger clumps for further filtration.
